  "behavior": [
    "Loose curves retain their converted NURBS degree, knots, control count and weights. Greville locations retain one-sided full-order knots and periodic station/control ordering.",
    "Existing faer and usd-brep fixed-row/nonuniform periodic solvers reconstruct controls. Exact rational station residuals admit output, including rejection of error hidden by rounded evaluation.",
    "Finite edit-point queries respect trims and complete misses. Planar directional hits reuse the shared affine plane transform; curved hits retain the existing intersector.",
    "Complete ordered projection hit branches require consistent facing at stations; misses, branch-count changes and ambiguous seams do not invent partial interpolation.",
    "App Loose preferences are independent for Project and Pull. Both reuse target/source picking, temporary ranges, layers, deletion, infinite planes and atomic history.",
    "Optional loose booleans extend four existing Python operations. True retains full output definitions and selects public Rhino Loose overloads; false keeps prior response shapes and SDK calls."
  ],
