  "limitations": [
    "Finite curve inputs require clamped non-periodic layout or exact periodic tails, common-sign weights, degree <=17 and <=1000 stored controls. Degenerate stations, ill-conditioned solves and exhausted shared certificate budgets decline.",
    "Only reconstructed requested station positions are certified. Source evaluation and target point queries retain existing numerical policies. Curves may leave surfaces or cross holes between edit points.",
    "Branch association and wrap checks are discrete and conservative, not whole-curve topology certificates. Global closest choice and native command/getter/metadata parity remain unqualified.",
    "The existing closed-triangle mesh query can reject a rounded Greville point just outside a boundary. That observed miss remains in the fixture; native tolerance parity is unresolved.",
    "Fresh Rhino observations are unavailable because of the existing Wine SSPI issue. Public Loose SDK recipes require suitable Rhino overloads (8.17 or newer); host-independent mocks do not qualify live SDK execution.",
    "No comparative performance qualification is claimed. Grip/edit-point subobject input, SubD and broader subobject selection remain pending."
  ],
